      {
        "number": 10,
        "internalPageId": 10,
        "title": "Language Targets",
        "visibleTexts": [
          "Language Targets",
          "Aspects Examples 1 Talk about infancy experiences. We used to have a baseball team in our street back in the 80s. 2 State old bad habits. John used to smoke a lot but he stopped a few months ago. 3 Define people’s old conditions. Jake looks great, He used to wear messy hair but not anymore. 4 Express customs people have They are used to drink coffee only in the mornings.",
          "When using past simple to talk about habits, we may be talking about different aspects or functions.",
          "TO CONSIDER Time phrases are very important, no matter the function or aspect covered; sometimes, they determine the context"
        ],
        "links": [],
