      {
        "number": 13,
        "internalPageId": 14,
        "title": "Memories! I always remember my childhood. I used to spend hours with my friends nearby the river swimming, playing and sometimes camping. We used to go there almost every Saturday to play at the tree house and to listen to good music. I have to admit that we used to be very noisy kids; however, we used to be good kids and we never made anything terrible…well, we used to ring doorbells to our neighbors so we were not angels either. I’d wish those times to be back, kids now do not enjoy life since technology has overtaken them; I truly think we had the greatest childhood.",
        "visibleTexts": [
          "Memories! I always remember my childhood. I used to spend hours with my friends nearby the river swimming, playing and sometimes camping. We used to go there almost every Saturday to play at the tree house and to listen to good music. I have to admit that we used to be very noisy kids; however, we used to be good kids and we never made anything terrible…well, we used to ring doorbells to our neighbors so we were not angels either. I’d wish those times to be back, kids now do not enjoy life since technology has overtaken them; I truly think we had the greatest childhood.",
          "C. Read the following paragraph and state if the sentences are true (T) or false (F). After that, read the paragraph aloud to your teacher.",
          "1. He never remembers his childhood. (T) (F) 2. He used to spend hours near the lake. (T) (F) 3. They used to go camping too. (T) (F) 4. They used to go there every Saturday. (T) (F)",
          "5. They used to read books at the tree house. (T) (F) 6. They used to be bad kids. (T) (F) 7. They didn’t use to ring doorbells. (T) (F) 8. He considers they had the greatest childhood. (T) (F)"
        ],
